{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>For</b> — Do not think that when HaShem refrains from judging, there is in the east or west or in the desert mountains — that is, opposite the land of Israel — anyone who will save you. And Rabbi Moses said: For everything that exists in the east or the west is all under HaShem's dominion. And some say: For this is an allusion to the science of the constellations, those who reckon that the good and the evil and the honor and the disgrace that come upon a man — all of it is in the arrangement of the stars, and the first pillar is the eastern one; also the western, also the southern, which is opposite the desert mountains — these are the ones that rule over all mankind. And he did not mention the fourth pillar because it has no power, on account of being beneath the earth."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 75, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:36.148155520Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}